{"builder":"Goal: one pull request on suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test that adds a new workspace packages/jsonl-lint and meets every acceptance line of https://github.com/suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test/issues/102. Today packages/ does not exist; the root package.json already declares workspaces packages/* and its test script runs npm test --workspaces --if-present; .github/workflows/test.yml runs npm ci then npm test on Node 22.\n\nSteps:\n1. Create packages/jsonl-lint/package.json: name \"jsonl-lint\", \"type\": \"module\", \"scripts\": { \"test\": \"node --test\" }, a \"bin\": { \"jsonl-lint\": \"bin/jsonl-lint.js\" }, engines node >=22, and no \"dependencies\" (no runtime dependencies; avoid devDependencies too, node:test needs none).\n2. Create packages/jsonl-lint/src/index.js (plain ES module, no deps) exporting lint(text) that returns an array of { line, error } objects, one per row that is not valid JSON:\n   - split the text on \\n (also strip a trailing \\r so CRLF files work);\n   - line numbers are 1-based and count every physical line, including blank ones;\n   - skip lines that are empty or whitespace only;\n   - a trailing newline at the end of the file does not create an extra row, but a last line with no terminating newline is still a row and is checked (a torn/truncated last row must be reported);\n   - error is the JSON.parse error message string;\n   - return [] when every row is valid.\n3. Create packages/jsonl-lint/bin/jsonl-lint.js with a #!/usr/bin/env node shebang (make it executable, chmod +x, and commit the mode). Behaviour: with no argument, print a usage message to stderr and exit 2. If the file cannot be read (missing, ENOENT, or other read error), print a message to stderr and exit 2. Otherwise read the file as utf8, call lint, print one line per finding to stdout in exactly the form <file>:<line>: <error> (the file argument as given), exit 1 if there was any finding and 0 if none. Nothing goes to stdout for a clean file.\n4. Create packages/jsonl-lint/test/ with node:test tests (e.g. test/lint.test.js; make sure `node --test` run from packages/jsonl-lint discovers them — files under test/ ending .test.js are found by default). Cover, at minimum, both through lint() and through the CLI (spawn process.execPath with bin/jsonl-lint.js via node:child_process, using temp files from node:fs/os):\n   - a clean file: lint returns [], CLI exits 0 with empty stdout;\n   - a bad middle row: e.g. 3 rows with row 2 broken, reported as line 2, CLI prints <file>:2: ... and exits 1;\n   - a torn last row with no trailing newline (e.g. '{\"a\":1}\\n{\"b\":' ), reported at its line number;\n   - blank lines: blank/whitespace lines are skipped and do not shift numbering (a bad row after blanks keeps its physical 1-based line number);\n   - exit codes: 0 clean, 1 findings, 2 for a missing file and 2 for no argument, and that the exit-2 cases write to stderr.\n5. Create packages/jsonl-lint/README.md: what the tool does, usage (node packages/jsonl-lint/bin/jsonl-lint.js <file>), the output format, exit codes 0/1/2, and the lint(text) API.\n6. Update the root README.md: replace the \"No tools yet: packages/ is empty\" bullet under \"What is here\" with a bullet listing packages/jsonl-lint and a one-line description.\n7. Run `npm install` at the repo root so package-lock.json records the new workspace, and commit the updated package-lock.json — otherwise `npm ci` in the test workflow fails. Then run `npm ci && npm test` at the root and confirm it passes and that the jsonl-lint tests actually ran.\n8. Manually smoke-test the CLI: a clean file (exit 0), a file with a bad middle row and a torn last row (two lines of output, exit 1), a missing path (stderr, exit 2), no argument (stderr, exit 2).\n9. Commit everything on your branch, push, and open one pull request to the default branch whose body contains the line: Closes https://github.com/suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test/issues/102\n10. Wait for the test workflow (the \"test\" check from .github/workflows/test.yml) to finish on the PR head; if it fails, read the log, fix, push again, until it is green. Do not open a second PR.","verifier":"Check out the pull request's head commit and, from the repository root, run `npm ci` first. Make temp files outside the repo (e.g. under mktemp -d). There is one check per acceptance line, in order.\n\nCheck 1 — \"packages/jsonl-lint/bin/jsonl-lint.js <file> prints <file>:<line>: <error> for every row that is not valid JSON (1-based lines, blank lines skipped, an unterminated last line checked) and exits 1 if any, 0 if none\".\nRun: create clean.jsonl with printf '{\"a\":1}\\n\\n[2]\\n' and bad.jsonl with printf '{\"a\":1}\\n{oops\\n\\n   \\n{\"b\":2}\\n{\"c\":' (bad row at line 2, blank lines 3–4, unterminated bad last row at line 6). Run `node packages/jsonl-lint/bin/jsonl-lint.js clean.jsonl; echo $?` and the same for bad.jsonl (pass the path exactly as you print it below).\nPASS: clean.jsonl prints no <file>:<line>: lines and exits 0; bad.jsonl prints a line starting `<path>:2: ` followed by an error text and a line starting `<path>:6: ` followed by an error text, prints no such line for any valid or blank line, and exits 1.\nFAIL: any other exit status, a missing report for line 2 or line 6, wrong (e.g. 0-based or blank-skipping-shifted) line numbers, a report for a blank or valid line, or output not in the <file>:<line>: <error> form.\n\nCheck 2 — \"A missing file or no argument prints to stderr and exits 2\".\nRun: `node packages/jsonl-lint/bin/jsonl-lint.js /nonexistent/x.jsonl >out 2>err; echo $?` and `node packages/jsonl-lint/bin/jsonl-lint.js >out 2>err; echo $?`, inspecting err each time.\nPASS: both exit 2 and both write something non-empty to stderr.\nFAIL: either exits with any other status or writes nothing to stderr.\n\nCheck 3 — \"packages/jsonl-lint/src/index.js exports lint(text) returning [{ line, error }]\".\nRun: `node --input-type=module -e \"import { lint } from './packages/jsonl-lint/src/index.js'; console.log(JSON.stringify(lint('{\\\"a\\\":1}\\nnope\\n'))); console.log(JSON.stringify(lint('{\\\"a\\\":1}\\n')));\"`.\nPASS: lint is a named export; the first call returns an array with one object that has a line property equal to 2 and an error property; the second returns an empty array.\nFAIL: import fails, lint is not exported, the result is not an array, or the objects lack line or error.\n\nCheck 4 — \"The workspace has its own package.json (jsonl-lint, type module, test script node --test), no runtime dependencies, and node:test tests for a clean file, a bad middle row, a torn last row, blank lines and the exit codes\".\nRun: read packages/jsonl-lint/package.json; run `npm test -w packages/jsonl-lint` (or `cd packages/jsonl-lint && npm test`); read the test files it runs.\nPASS: package.json has name jsonl-lint, type module, a test script that runs node --test, and no non-empty dependencies field; the tests run and pass; and the tests, using node:test, include cases for a clean file, a bad middle row, a torn (unterminated) last row, blank lines, and the CLI exit codes.\nFAIL: any of those fields is wrong or missing, there are runtime dependencies, the tests fail or do not run, or any of the five listed cases has no test.\n\nCheck 5 — \"packages/jsonl-lint/README.md exists and the root README lists the tool\".\nRun: `test -f packages/jsonl-lint/README.md && echo ok`; read README.md at the root.\nPASS: the file exists and the root README.md mentions jsonl-lint as a tool in the repo.\nFAIL: the file is missing or the root README does not list jsonl-lint.\n\nCheck 6 — \"The change is one PR on suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test whose body says Closes https://github.com/suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test/issues/102, and npm test and the test workflow are green at its head\".\nRun: `gh pr view <pr> --repo suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test --json body,headRefOid,url`; `gh pr list --repo suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test --state open --search 102` to see whether other PRs exist for this issue; at the head run `npm ci && npm test` at the repo root; read the test workflow's check on the head commit with `gh pr checks <pr> --repo suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test` (or gh run list --commit <headRefOid>).\nPASS: the PR is on suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test, its body contains Closes https://github.com/suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test/issues/102, the change is in this single PR, npm test at the head passes, and the test workflow's check for the head commit concluded success.\nFAIL: the body lacks that text, the change is split across PRs, npm test fails at the head, or the test workflow is failing, missing, or not finished for the head commit (if still running, wait for it before deciding).\n\nAdvisory (not pass/fail conditions):\n- Check that package-lock.json includes the new workspace so `npm ci` works in CI.\n- Check that the <error> text is the JSON.parse message, that a CRLF file is linted cleanly, and that a trailing newline does not add a phantom row.\n- Check bin/jsonl-lint.js has a shebang and executable mode, and that nothing is written to stdout for the exit-2 cases."}